id: pm-namespace-recovery-delivery
title: Deliver unambiguous registry-derived namespace recovery across installed Node and Bun consumers
description: "Execution child of the canonical recovery feature for GH-1433. Derive a canonical help retry for a misplaced registered namespace suffix, refuse ambiguous or unavailable routes and preserve nonempty item/history bytes through real installed npm/npx and Bun/bunx consumers. The parent retains the complete recovery-census programme."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-10T18:34:13.033Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-11T01:04:32.117Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-11T01:04:31.536Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-11T01:04:31.536Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Public SDK resolver uses installed canonical identity and refuses ambiguity; CLI JSON and text recommend inspection while preserving usage failure; real nonempty source and packed npx/bunx controls preserve authoritative bytes; existing discovery behavior and generated surface gates remain intact
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make a refused namespace mistake recoverable without guessing or executing a mutation
value: Agents discover the intended registered command from a concise executable refusal
why_now: Published 2026.10.10 reproducibly omits canonical update help for item update
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "Delivered longest unambiguous installed-suffix recovery across complete registered namespaces, with global flag/value and operand boundaries, tracker/extension-preserving executable help, portable Windows launchers and independent required full consumer acceptance. Root namespace admission now shares the same first-iteration SDK check as deeper prefixes instead of duplicating it before the loop."
expected_result: "Nested canonical help uses one registered-prefix admission path, refuses unknown or ambiguous routes, preserves tracker and extension policy, and passes all required analyzers and renewed full review."
actual_result: "Current complete static/typecheck, 59 linked assertions plus one Windows-only skip, and serialized nine-package npx/Bun/bunx/SDK consumers pass unchanged limits. Prior head 4a32b2aff passed all five hosted workflows and exact full coverage; its sole failed required context reported one new DeepScan issue without details. Next-head DeepScan and fresh full review remain mandatory before merge; no analyzer waiver or unverified cause is claimed."
