comments[26]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-10T18:34:13.033Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: strict live 2918-item all-status census and request-specific searches have no focused namespace-recovery execution child. Existing pm-f05lsg remains the canonical programme/report owner. This Task records the bounded delivery and does not duplicate that feature or its complete census acceptance. Prior read-recovery and alias-help deliveries remain completed."
  "2026-10-10T19:03:22.385Z","harness:codex","Installed current-artifact acceptance passed: npm install plus both npx bin identities, installed npx canonical retries, bunx --bun canonical retries, trusted measurement retry with an executed node:assert check, authoritative item/history byte preservation, nine bundled packages and TypeScript SDK consumer. Boundary-focused Node24 rerun passed96 tests, including docs reachability, unchanged MCP task timing, and existing flag-help ceilings. Full coverage and broad static final receipts are pending; no product, help-token, latency or RSS budget was increased."
  "2026-10-10T19:03:23.509Z","harness:codex","Public dependency census: all current/wanted versions agree. New latest @types/node26.6.5, jscpd5.4.1, typescript-eslint8.71.1, TOON4.4.0, Knip6.41.0 and marked18.1.0 were published1.0-5.2days ago and are below the unchanged seven-day adoption window. Sentry11.6.0 is2.2days old and retains canonical migration pm-t3jxjj; Vitest/coverage5.0.3 retain pm-fokyhh and TypeScript7.0.2 retains pm-do5b. pnpm audit found zero known vulnerabilities, GitHub open PR/Dependabot/code/secret inventories were empty at intake, and every open issue had a canonical PM-link comment."
  "2026-10-10T19:05:30.053Z","harness:codex","Remaining public major candidate npm-package-arg14.0.0 requires Node^22.22.2 or^24.15.0 or>=26, which excludes the published pm-cli minimum22.18.0; no engine-policy violation is adopted. Installed CodSpeed5.7.1 still accepts Vitest^3.2 or^4 and installed typescript-eslint8.71.0 still accepts TypeScript>=4.8.4 <6.1.0. The canonical migration conditions were rechecked live. Sentry dashboard inspection through Chrome was attempted, but the browser connection became unavailable; fresh authenticated Sentry CLI/API receipts remain the verified evidence source."
  "2026-10-10T19:47:05.687Z","harness:codex","Final implementation and installed acceptance pass. The public SDK resolver returns only a unique canonical installed command and CLI refusals advertise help tokens without executing a mutation. Direct, installed npx and Bun/bunx checks preserve authoritative item/history bytes for help and mutating namespace refusals and execute the canonical help retry. Linked17-test evidence and post-extraction144-test focused verification pass; the complete earlier10111-test suite had exact coverage. All static components and serialized packed acceptance pass. A concurrent distribution-consumer rebuild failure is separately recorded under the release capability; the existing build serialization and runtime staging deliveries remain completed."
  "2026-10-10T19:50:51.011Z","harness:codex","Reviewed delivery: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1436 addresses GitHub1433 with the public SDK resolver and real installed refusal/retry proof. Initial source commit a279913ba is locally verified, closure and the generated Unreleased entry are included, and the canonical parent retains the broader uncovered refusal census. Final-head CI and review are required before merge."
  "2026-10-10T20:08:47.991Z","harness:codex",PR #1436 review at 2e59d2e897f253cf40ce26f1bc017b17aadee409 verified that canonical extension help retry arguments lose explicitly selected tracker scope. Reopened to preserve bootstrap --pm-path in executable help guidance and clarify that retry tokens are arguments to the pm executable.
  "2026-10-10T20:13:28.175Z","harness:codex","The new selected-tracker extension regression also reproduced a bootstrap-help path bug: help reduced a refused multi-token path to its leaf and omitted argv when deriving recovery. The canonical route was therefore absent even before tracker preservation. Fix both help entry points to retain the full refused path, alongside scoped retry tokens; negative control confirmed extension help fails from the unrelated default tracker."
  "2026-10-10T20:23:03.715Z","harness:codex","Review regressions now cover a package installed in the explicitly selected tracker while PM_PATH points elsewhere: advertised canonical help succeeds with selected scope, the unscoped command fails, and explicit --no-extensions suppresses the installed route. Refused help retains the full namespace path; item/history preservation and SDK/CLI refusal behavior passed the 366-test focused review suite."
  "2026-10-10T20:35:02.606Z","harness:codex","Review remediation verified: the linked canonical recovery and real-CLI integration run passes 18 tests, including a nonempty explicitly selected extension tracker, a different default tracker, and --no-extensions suppression. Refused requests preserve authoritative item/history bytes. Both packed npx and bunx consumers replay scoped canonical help successfully. Full static gates pass with unchanged budgets; final-head CI/review remains a required merge condition."
  "2026-10-10T20:46:44.522Z","harness:codex","Final self-review found a remaining boundary to verify: selected --pm-path is copied raw, so a relative tracker path in retry arguments changes meaning when executed from another working directory. The live closed delivery record requires selected-tracker replay from any working directory; reopen this unmerged delivery to resolve explicit tracker scope to its absolute SDK root and prove the relative-path case."
  "2026-10-10T20:50:32.889Z","harness:codex","The relative-path negative control failed at 3b7dafa24 as expected: .agents/pm was advertised instead of the selected absolute tracker. Resolving the explicit path with the existing SDK resolvePmRoot fixes replay. All 18 linked namespace tests now pass while executing the advertised extension help from a different cwd/default tracker; packed npx and bunx also pass with a relative tracker selection and 9 packages. ESLint/build pass; no new API, budget or trust-policy change was needed."
  "2026-10-10T20:57:06.341Z","harness:codex","CI receipt for published head 3b7dafa24: all 67,922 statements, 64,616 lines and 13,996 functions are covered; exactly one of 52,009 branches was uncovered, at commander-usage.ts scoped retry. This is the real executable/source instrumentation boundary, not a behavior failure or a lowered threshold. The existing installed-extension integration now asserts source/executable retry parity for the same relative path and passes all 18 linked tests. Fresh final-head exact coverage remains mandatory before merge."
  "2026-10-10T21:09:15.092Z","harness:codex",Final-head 843b78169 passed all26 required contexts with no missing gates or unresolved threads. CodeRabbit completed a full base-to-head review with no actionable code comments; its docstring check reports79.55percent across44 touched functions. Reopen this unmerged delivery solely to document the canonical recovery fallback/example ordering before a fresh review. The previously acknowledged BIG-PR scope warning remains intentional under the project request.
  "2026-10-10T21:10:50.747Z","harness:codex","Review documentation improvement: canonical fallback namespaces and concrete-help ordering now have semantic docstrings, and the public guidance builder explains inspection-only scope-preserving behavior. The reviewed filler baseline decreases11to10 for commander-usage; no ceiling increases. Build, ESLint, docstring gate and all18 linked tests pass. Fresh843b CI artifact confirms67922statements,64616lines,13996functions and52009branches all covered100percent; full JUnit10115tests has zero failures/errors. The next final head still requires fresh CI and full review."
  "2026-10-10T22:18:28.306Z","harness:codex","PR #1436 final-head review https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1436#pullrequestreview-5480989632: The packed recovery helper and smoke runner launch Windows .cmd files directly. Node requires a command interpreter for these shims; use the existing vetted cross-spawn7.0.6 version as a direct dev dependency for argument-safe portable launch and run the real complete packed acceptance in the required Windows job."
  "2026-10-10T22:50:35.587Z","harness:codex","Final-control review remediation: both installed-recovery and packed-smoke executors use pinned mature cross-spawn 7.0.6, added only as a direct development dependency. Native Windows selection distinguishes npm.cmd/npx.cmd from bunx.exe, confirmed by official Bun source. Linux packed npm/npx and Bun/bunx acceptance passes with nine bundled packages, real byte-preserving refusals, executable measurement recovery and SDK type/runtime consumers. Linked namespace and launcher tests pass. Windows CI now runs a real .cmd shim located in a spaced path, a direct-spawn negative control and full packed npm/npx/Bun/bunx acceptance with pinned Bun 1.4.0; hosted Windows proof remains pending on the next head. Job timeout grows from 12 to 20 minutes to cover this additional matrix, with no product or coverage budget changes. Audit, dependency cooldown, zero duplication, typecheck and all static gates pass."
  "2026-10-10T23:21:47.097Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1436#pullrequestreview-5481136765 found two valid remaining presentation boundaries: explicit --no-extensions is dropped by canonical retry argv, and the first displayed help example omits selected-tracker scope even though tokenized recovery retains it. Windows run 38093339636 completed real shim/source regression tests and the full nine-package npm/npx/Bun/bunx/SDK acceptance at 23:19 UTC; the combined regression job then timed out during later history tests. Move the already required full Windows consumer acceptance to the existing required Windows/Node24 packed-consumer matrix cell, retaining all checks and a 20-minute ceiling, and restore the regression job to its prior 12-minute bound. No product, coverage, duplication or dependency safety ratchets change."
  "2026-10-10T23:39:07.164Z","harness:codex","Both new review omissions are confirmed by independent pre-fix negatives: explicit --no-extensions drops from retry argv, and the displayed first extension-help example omits --pm-path despite scoped tokenized recovery. Current focused tests pass 42 assertions plus one native-Windows-only skip. Canonical help now uses one policy-preserving retry constructor and renders its first example from the same tokens. Full static and typecheck pass without raising complexity, duplication, latency, RSS, control or coverage limits. Windows full packed acceptance remains intact in the existing required Windows/Node24 first-run matrix cell, with pinned pnpm/Bun and frozen dependencies; only that cell receives a 20-minute deadline, while other packed cells retain 10 minutes and source/history regression returns to 12 minutes. Prior 30e4d5b full CI coverage was exact 100 percent over 67939 statements, 64633 lines, 14001 functions and 52040 branches; fresh head checks remain required before merge."
  "2026-10-10T23:41:18.889Z","harness:codex","Final second-review remediation verification: serialized current-source npx/Bun packed acceptance passes nine packages and the installed SDK type/runtime consumers, including preserved --no-extensions in replayed canonical help. Linked namespace, launcher and existing workflow-contract tests all pass; both pre-fix help-display negatives fail as expected. Full static/typecheck and focused docs-link gates pass with unchanged source ratchets. Required names and all six packed matrix cells remain present; the Windows/Node24 full consumer suite now has its own existing required check and a 20-minute bound, independent from the unchanged 12-minute source/history check. Next-head CI and fresh included full review remain merge requirements."
  "2026-10-11T00:11:20.571Z","harness:codex","Review 5481282084 covers base c233923 through 25fcde173 and identifies an immediate-child-only reconstruction in commander-usage.ts. Current head CI is green in all 26 required contexts, both Windows jobs really executed successfully, and coverage is exact 100 percent over 67942 statements, 64635 lines, 14002 functions and 52044 branches (10127 passed, 3 skipped). Only this namespace delivery is reopened and actively claimed; measurement and runner deliveries remain closed/released. Repair will use registered command prefixes so flags and operands cannot become fabricated namespace tokens, with a pre-fix negative and executable/source regression."
  "2026-10-11T00:14:36.470Z","harness:codex","Confirmed pre-fix negative: nested workspace/config/update with an author value equal to the refused leaf produces no canonical retry. The repaired scanner retains only registered prefixes, skips contract-defined global flags/values, stops at the refused leaf, and preserves fallback behavior for missing commands, terminators and operands. Current focused source/executable tests pass 20 with one native-Windows-only skip, including real three-token extension-help recovery replayed from another tracker. An initial ordinary extension fixture reached a different lazy-activation/too-many-arguments refusal; it was corrected to explicitly request the help path under test and is not presented as a negative for this fix. Typecheck passes; full static, linked verification and serialized packed consumers are next."
  "2026-10-11T00:23:42.889Z","harness:codex","The review's root-only nested case also exposed the SDK resolver's one-prefix limitation: independent pre-fix tests fail for workspace config update when only root update is available. The SDK now considers exact suffixes longest first, crossing only registered prefixes; ambiguity at a longer suffix terminates recovery instead of guessing a shorter command. Tests also preserve unavailable-prefix refusal and prefer config update when that longer route exists. Current focused transport/SDK tests pass 20 with one native-Windows-only skip; docs explain the bounded semantics. Final typecheck/static rerun follows this public behavioral repair before serialized packed and linked proof."
  "2026-10-11T00:33:38.102Z","harness:codex","Final nested recovery repair passes typecheck and the complete static pipeline, including unchanged qualified performance controls and 329 killed plus 7 equivalent bounded mutants (zero failures). All three linked commands pass: 20 canonical/transport assertions plus one Windows-only skip, 23 portable launcher assertions and 16 workflow assertions. Serialized current packed acceptance passes nine bundled packages, npx/Bun/bunx and installed SDK types/runtime consumers. Docs links pass. Both independent pre-fix negatives are retained as private evidence, and authoritative item/history preservation remains tested. Fresh next-head full CI and included full review remain required before merge."
  "2026-10-11T00:54:03.468Z","harness:codex","Fresh 4a32b2aff hosted CI, Security/Script Quality, Docs, CodeQL and CodSpeed all succeed; the native watcher reports DeepScan as the sole failed required context (1 new and 0 fixed issues). GitHub exposes no DeepScan check-run annotations, and a direct Chrome Computer Use report-open attempt fails because the selected browser is unavailable. The newly generalized SDK resolver redundantly checks the root namespace both before its loop and at namespaceLength=1. Remove the duplicated outer check while preserving first-iteration admission and all existing behavioral proof; validate the next DeepScan result before attributing the external finding. No analyzer exclusion or policy bypass is authorized. The old-head review timer is stopped before any quota-consuming stale review."
  "2026-10-11T01:04:30.868Z","harness:codex","The root admission simplification passes complete static/typecheck without changed ratchets, 59 linked assertions plus one native-Windows-only skip, and serialized nine-package npx/Bun/bunx/installed-SDK packed acceptance. Missing roots remain refused by the first loop iteration, deeper unregistered prefixes remain refused, and ambiguous longer matches do not fall back. Prior 4a32b2aff coverage artifact is exact 100 percent over 67955 statements, 64644 lines, 14002 functions and 52050 branches with 10128 passing tests and 3 skips. The external DeepScan rule remains undisclosed through GitHub and Chrome is unavailable; the next required analyzer result and full review gate merge, with no waiver or asserted causal attribution."
